        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1890,
        "paragraph_id": "1F2E8BBB",
        "text": "Figure 5.2 \t\t\tControl volume u-momentum balance and definition of fluxes"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 89308,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4366,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1892,
        "paragraph_id": "611EE268",
        "text": "In (C.9) and (C.10) the procedure for computing the u-momentum balance is outlined. The discharges in the u-points are computed by multiplying the velocity in the u- or v-point by the water depth at that point. These discharges are then interpolated to the borders of the control volume around the u-point. The difference Δa in grid orientation between the incoming cell and the u-point is computed and used to compute the component of the incoming velocity in the local u-direction, from the left and right side of the control volume."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 89502,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4370,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1896,
        "paragraph_id": "3EF27F40",
        "text": "The same is done for the top and bottom of the control volume, based on the discharges in v-direction:"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
